{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1094890-a-death-question","id":1094890,"title":"A death question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-20T10:32:59-07:00","id":1094890,"title":"A death question","content":"I was thinking about a peculiar set up for a chronicle<br /> <br /> <br /> What could be the greatest mistake that THE DEATH could do?<br /> <br /> Imagine the death like a person, like the Death of the comic book sand man<br /> <br /> What could be a mistake, an error, a misunderstanding that can be heavy on her soul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12508-elanconnor","name":"ElanConnor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T20:25:33-07:00","id":1095005,"title":"","content":"Missing an appointment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T21:59:30-07:00","id":1095022,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure there would be an incarnate Death like that in Scion. The whole point of the game is Pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T05:42:58-07:00","id":1095096,"title":"","content":"That's a good point. Although if you made a Christian pantheon then the modern Death would be the child of Lucifer and his daughter Chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T06:10:54-07:00","id":1095104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>racain23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1094890-a-death-question?p=1095096#post1095096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good point. Although if you made a Christian pantheon then the modern Death would be the child of Lucifer and his daughter Chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't Death be a child of either the Lion of Judah or Yahweh since the entity specifically with the name of Death is in the Fourth Seal and released by the Lamb (also Chaos isn't an entity in Christianity)?<br /> <br /> It would be amusing if you used the translation which had Hades with him. I like to imagine the two made a deal for eons ago before Death got sealed, letting Death use various wild beasts like Cerberus in his assault on the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T06:34:47-07:00","id":1095109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>racain23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1094890-a-death-question?p=1095096#post1095096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good point. Although if you made a Christian pantheon then the modern Death would be the child of Lucifer and his daughter Chaos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that Paradise Lost? And Satan's daughter named Sin, not Chaos in that work?<br /> <br /> If we do include Paradise Lost, though, we have some... <i>interesting </i>entities to put in Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T11:06:21-07:00","id":1095176,"title":"","content":"I feel like the modern interpretation of Death, The Reaper, etc, would make a good icon for a scion to latch themselves onto in building their own legend, as well. Similar to some of the discussion in other threads about scions forming an Americana pantheon. Would be interesting to see a whole pantheon of modern concept personifications. The Reaper, father time, mother nature, etc. Of course they'd all be to some extent pastiches of other mythologies with some pop culture thrown in, but that doesn't seem like it'd be a problem for scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T22:12:08-07:00","id":1096608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1094890-a-death-question?p=1095109#post1095109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that Paradise Lost? And Satan's daughter named Sin, not Chaos in that work?<br /> <br /> If we do include Paradise Lost, though, we have some... <i>interesting </i>entities to put in Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is, and I apologise for my mistake. Milo V3, is that from revelations, or some other source? I'm a big fan of christian mythology, but I always struggle to find &quot;offical&quot; sources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-24T22:53:09-07:00","id":1096620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>racain23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1094890-a-death-question?p=1096608#post1096608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Milo V3, is that from revelations, or some other source? I'm a big fan of christian mythology, but I always struggle to find &quot;offical&quot; sources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it's from Revelations chapter 6. Should be easy to locate online, just google four horsemen. Death is the only horsemen which has a name, and is also the only horsmen who does not carry an object (... which is why he should not be depicted with a scythe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T03:30:32-07:00","id":1096660,"title":"","content":"My understanding was that the sythe was a pre-Christian holdover, but I have nothing concrete to back it up. I have read through revelations, but I've always struggled to make coherent sense of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T09:53:36-07:00","id":1096781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>racain23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1094890-a-death-question?p=1096660#post1096660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding was that the sythe was a pre-Christian holdover, but I have nothing concrete to back it up. I have read through revelations, but I've always struggled to make coherent sense of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would actually suggest the Scythe not being pre-Christian, but a later Christian change in their iconography. The Four Horsemen have a very interesting relationship in their depictions over time, with Revelations being about third century CE, and being carried through Christian popular culture through then. I don't know of a lot of places where a Scythe developed into a piece of death iconography asides from The Horsemen, not anywhere in Europe until the Black Death at least where Death picks it up in popular depiction.<br /> <br /> For example, there becomes a divide in Western and Eastern Europe over the identity of one of the Horsemen. In Western Europe, Conquest is replaced by Pestilence, where Eastern Europe keeps Conquest. There is about a thousand years for popular religious belief to change and dance over this period, and I don't think the Scythe shows up on Death until the arrival of the Black Plague in Western Europe. At this point, Conquest is faded out for Pestilence, and I believe the idea of Death clearing lives like wheat becomes more common, and thus the Scythe. Of course, all of this is in essentially 'Pop-Religion,' and it doesn't always become cannonical. For example, Pestilence still is not one of the Four Horsemen in traditional Catholic systems, but the general public never remembers Conquest.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T20:34:35-07:00","id":1096968,"title":"","content":"I guess some might prefer Pestilence because Conquest feels kinda redundant with War. Of course, they all lead to Death, so it is not much of an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-25T22:51:47-07:00","id":1096988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1094890-a-death-question?p=1096968#post1096968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess some might prefer Pestilence because Conquest feels kinda redundant with War. Of course, they all lead to Death, so it is not much of an issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revelations is so incredibly symbolical and weird that even theologians have enormous trouble interpreting it. Some make a distinction between Conquest as a process of domination, and War as all blood and gore. Some say Conquest is war between nations, while War represents civil war. Some say that the horseman on the white horse is Jesus Christ, re-conquering the world spiritually on Judgement Day. And what the hell does &quot;all Hades following Death&quot; mean? Information is slim, with the Horsemen just covering a few lines in that whole big book, then never appearing again.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm always a fan of making the horseman on the white horse Pollution <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For more Abrahamic mythology on Death, one could also consider the well-known Islamic depiction of the angel of death, Azrael, a terrible being with innumerable eyes and tongues. Whenever he claims a person's life, one eye closes, and when all his eyes are closed and the end of the world arrives, Azrael himself will die. Then there is the death of the firstborns in Exodus and some other passages in the Old Testament alluding to a personified Death - in Exodus, it actually says that God himself walks through Egypt to bring death, but as with Jacob wrestling with God, Jewish and Christian commentary later explains that as an angel having acted as representative of God in these situations. The Book of Job then mentions a whole class of minor angels of death and fate, called <i>memitim</i> in Hebrew. So whether one wishes to make a composite figure out of that or several separate ones, there is enough material for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T03:16:29-07:00","id":1097062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1094890-a-death-question?p=1095022#post1095022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure there would be an incarnate Death like that in Scion. The whole point of the game is Pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanatos (spelling) for the greeks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T05:09:36-07:00","id":1097079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>racain23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1094890-a-death-question?p=1097062#post1097062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanatos (spelling) for the greeks</div> </div> </div> </div>There are of course deities that embody death in every pantheon... They're kind of a universal thing, pretty much. I think what Lex was specifically referring to was some kind of pan cultural embodiment of Death in the vein of Sandman or Discworld's Death, that's a little out of place in a Scion world that focuses on the Pantheons (your shards may vary).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-26T23:05:26-07:00","id":1097433,"title":"","content":"In 1e, you could use the same mechanic that brought about the abrahamic god to exlain a personification of death. The death of discworld is such a brilliant character, I find it hard to mentally exclude him from any fantasy setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5727-racain23","name":"racain23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}